adam.hartman@gmail.com wrote:
> What are my options for getting back on my god's good side?

It doesn't matter how many tiny monsters you offer, it only depends on a 
few big ones.

As a wizard spells are a good measure of your progress.

The ones I would check for would be in order:

Confuse Monsters:  If you've got this one then stack it until you run 
out of spell points then go melee with Magicbane.  Very few monsters can 
stand up to confusion plus the 'bane.  (It helps if Magicbane is exactly 
at +2.)

Magic Missile: Wizards have a bonus with this spell so you might even 
get away with wearing a shield.  Look for tricky bank shots that nail 
monsters before they get you and fire down along long worms for instant 
kills.

Identify: Sell gems to shopkeepers to buy protection from priests.

Cone of Cold: Lets you walk through some damp places down deep.

If you can advance to level 15 and polyself into a Succubus then you can 
walk through your quest with just a sleep spell.  Once that is complete 
you can switch your cloak.

